# cuts/v1.0.32/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.32. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.32.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, AND WHY IT NEARLY DID NOT.
#
# tests/test_rollforward_registry_pin.sh asserts that the NEWEST manifest has a
# resolvable cuts/<tag>/cut.env. Adding cut-manifests/v1.0.32.yaml without this
# file makes v1.0.32 the newest cut with no pins, and the gate dies with a parse
# error, preflight goes red, and the cut job is SKIPPED with nothing signed.
# Measured on this branch before this file was added: the test exited 1.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE TRAP THIS FILE IS THE SECOND VICTIM OF, RECORDED SO IT IS THE LAST
#
# v1.0.31's cut.env pinned CM051=f219eb0f and stated the invariant in its own
# words: "the pin must name a tree whose install.sh is the one in the DMG",
# with a closing instruction to RE-VERIFY the blob sha immediately before
# pushing the tag. That instruction was correct, was addressed to a human, and
# was not executed. Three commits touched install.sh after the pin was written
# -- #745, #748 and #751, which are precisely the [memory] blocker fixes -- and
# by 2026-08-16 the pin had diverged:
#
#     f219eb0:install.sh  689452950e35c9409be493be18a37505e1d76808   <- DEAD
#     main:install.sh     4f0c44e8d38aa06fb529c4299d62365cb3e03378   <- FIXED
#
# Cutting v1.0.31 from its own declared pin today would have shipped the
# crash-looping Hub that v1.0.31 exists to fix. Prose cannot fail closed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PIN BELOW IS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED
#
# CM051 names main at the time of writing. The blob comparison was run, not
# assumed, and the branch carrying this file does not touch install.sh (measured:
# 0 install.sh paths in the diff against the pinned ref), so the pin and the
# shipping tree agree by content and not merely by ordering:
#
#     CM051 pin       install.sh blob  4f0c44e8d38aa06fb529c4299d62365cb3e03378
#     this branch     install.sh blob  4f0c44e8d38aa06fb529c4299d62365cb3e03378
#
# RE-VERIFY IMMEDIATELY BEFORE PUSHING THE TAG, AFTER THE LAST MERGE, NOT
# BEFORE IT:
#
#     git rev-parse $CM051:install.sh
#     git rev-parse main:install.sh
#
# If they diverge, re-point CM051 to main and re-run. A pin chosen early and
# trusted is the fifth thing to burn a tag in this series.
# ============================================================================

# The daemon. Unchanged from v1.0.31 -- v1.0.32 rebuilds no daemon, because the
# blocker is install-side and the fix needs no re-sign or re-notarise.
DAEMON_COMMIT=723c682fd7b4

# The CM051 tree whose install.sh ships in the DMG. See the blob note above.
CM051=db631533dd24c13479c1f922438f6ceb83a4c1d7
